Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• `stn`: filter for the target station ( `'723758'` ).  
• `year`: restrict to the year 2009.  
• `mo`: restrict to the month October ( `'10'` ).  
• `da`: provides the calendar day; will be concatenated into a full date.  
• `temp`: mean (average) daily temperature; used for sorting by “warmest”.  

Typical filter conditions you will need  
• `stn = '723758'`  
• `year = '2009'`  
• `mo   = '10'`  
• `temp <> 9999.9`   -- exclude the “missing‑value” code  

Below are 10 different exploratory‑to‑final SQL queries (each limited to 20 rows where possible) showing how one can move from simple inspection to the required result.

```sql
-- 1. Description: Peek at the first 20 raw rows for the target station in 2009
SELECT *
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.gsod2009`
WHERE stn = '723758'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: List distinct year‑month combinations available for station 723758
SELECT DISTINCT year, mo
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.gsod2009`
WHERE stn = '723758'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Show 20 distinct station numbers that appear in the 2009 file
SELECT DISTINCT stn
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.gsod2009`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Count how many days were reported for each month for station 723758
SELECT mo, COUNT(*) AS days_reported
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.gsod2009`
WHERE stn = '723758'
GROUP BY mo
ORDER BY mo
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Retrieve temperatures for each day in October 2009 for the station
SELECT da, temp
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.gsod2009`
WHERE stn  = '723758'
  AND year = '2009'
  AND mo   = '10'
  AND temp <> 9999.9
ORDER BY da
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Compute average temperature (already mean) per day in October 2009
SELECT da,
       AVG(temp) AS avg_temp        -- AVG not really needed, but shows aggregation pattern
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.gsod2009`
WHERE stn  = '723758'
  AND year = '2009'
  AND mo   = '10'
  AND temp <> 9999.9
GROUP BY da
ORDER BY da
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Rank the warmest October 2009 days for station 723758 (top 20)
SELECT da,
       temp
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.gsod2009`
WHERE stn  = '723758'
  AND year = '2009'
  AND mo   = '10'
  AND temp <> 9999.9
ORDER BY temp DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Join station metadata to fetch station name and coordinates
SELECT s.usaf        AS station_id,
       s.name        AS station_name,
       s.lat, s.lon, s.state
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.stations` AS s
WHERE s.usaf = '723758'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Combine GSOD data with station table (name + temp) for October 2009
SELECT CONCAT(g.year, '-', g.mo, '-', g.da) AS yyyymmdd,
       g.temp,
       st.name AS station_name
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.gsod2009` AS g
LEFT JOIN `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.stations` AS st
       ON g.stn = st.usaf
WHERE g.stn     = '723758'
  AND g.year    = '2009'
  AND g.mo      = '10'
  AND g.temp   <> 9999.9
ORDER BY g.temp DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description (FINAL): Return the top‑3 warmest dates in October‑2009 for station 723758
SELECT
  CONCAT(g.year, '-', LPAD(g.mo, 2, '0'), '-', LPAD(g.da, 2, '0')) AS `YYYY-MM-DD`
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.gsod2009` AS g
WHERE g.stn   = '723758'
  AND g.year  = '2009'
  AND g.mo    = '10'
  AND g.temp <> 9999.9
ORDER BY g.temp DESC
LIMIT 3;
```

Running the last query will yield exactly the three October‑2009 dates (formatted YYYY‑MM‑DD) with the highest mean temperature for station 723758.
